    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1087">

                <pb facs="1129" n="1117" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg1117"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890E.01/5–2945: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister to Syria
                        and Lebanon</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wadsworth</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-31T19:00:00-04:00">May 31, 1945—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>162. Reurtel 161, May 29. Dept feels that it is for the Lebanese Govt alone to
                    determine countries to which it may make treaty proposals and that the matter is
                    not one in which this Govt could give advice with propriety.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
